From 63eacb6ae6823ad5f7091dd0cf04a816fd0967a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Iaroslav Voitovych <yaroslav.voytovych@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 01:17:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: hci_sync: Fix extended advertising duration
 overflow

hci_enable_ext_advertising_sync() computes the advertising set Duration
from the instance timeout in a u16. The timeout comes from MGMT Add
Advertising or Add Extended Advertising Parameters in seconds, so any
timeout above 65 s wraps: 66 s is sent as a Duration of 46 (460 ms) and
the instance is removed after less than half a second, 655 s becomes
65.17 s, and timeouts congruent to 0 or 6357 modulo 8192 encode
Duration 0, which the controller reads as no limit, so such an instance
is never removed.

Compute the duration in a u32 and limit the encoded value to the
field's maximum of 0xffff (655.35 s). Timeouts up to 655 s are now
passed exactly; longer ones end at 655.35 s instead of at an arbitrary
earlier time or never.

Fixes: 10bbffa3e88e ("Bluetooth: Fix using advertising instance duration as timeout")
Signed-off-by: Iaroslav Voitovych <yaroslav.voytovych@gmail.com>
---
 net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c b/net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c
index 9d829c20c3160..d4359653937c6 100644
--- a/net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c
+++ b/net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c
@@ -1699,11 +1699,11 @@ int hci_enable_ext_advertising_sync(struct hci_dev *hdev, u8 instance)
 	 * scheduling it.
 	 */
 	if (adv && adv->timeout) {
-		u16 duration = adv->mesh ? adv->timeout :
+		u32 duration = adv->mesh ? adv->timeout :
 					   adv->timeout * MSEC_PER_SEC;
 
-		/* Time = N * 10 ms */
-		set->duration = cpu_to_le16(duration / 10);
+		/* Time = N * 10 ms, at most 0xffff (655.35 s) */
+		set->duration = cpu_to_le16(min_t(u32, duration / 10, U16_MAX));
 	}
 
 	/* Track which instance owns the advertising set since the handle

